-- title:
--   Unramified Tate module forces formal étaleness of all levels
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an intermediate field $K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p$ (here $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ is `PadicAlgCl p`) which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and write $\mathcal{O}_K$ for [`PadicAlgCl.ringOfIntegers p K`](def/PadicAlgCl_RingOfIntegers.html#L11), the intersection of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ with $K$, viewed as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-subalgebra. Let $h$ be a natural number and let $Q$ be a $p$-divisible group over $\mathcal{O}_K$ of height $h$ in the sense of the project's structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a family of commutative rings $Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$, each a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathcal{O}_K$ that is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}_K$-module of rank $p^{vh}$, together with surjective coalgebra-algebra maps $Q.\mathrm{level}(v+1)\to Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$ whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$. Write $Q.\mathrm{Points}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ for the direct limit over $v$ of the groups of $\mathcal{O}_K$-algebra maps $Q.\mathrm{level}\,v\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ under convolution, and $\mathrm{TateModule}$ for the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in these points with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$, on which $\mathcal{O}_K$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ act componentwise by $\mathbb{Z}_p$-linear endomorphisms via `Q.tateModuleRep`. Assume that whenever $\sigma$ is a $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ lying in the inertia subgroup attached to the valuation subring [`padicIntegers p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) (the image of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}_p$), and $\tau$ is an $\mathcal{O}_K$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ with $\tau t=\sigma t$ for all $t$, then $\tau$ fixes every element of the Tate module. The conclusion is that for every natural number $v$ the $\mathcal{O}_K$-algebra $Q.\mathrm{level}\,v$ is formally étale.
--
--   This is the étaleness half of Tate's analysis of $p$-divisible groups over the ring of integers of a local field: a group whose $p$-adic Tate module is unramified has dimension $0$, hence all of its finite levels are étale. It feeds into the study of $p$-divisible groups attached to elliptic curves with unramified $p$-adic Tate module, being used in the derivation that the dual of each level kills the relevant elements under the norm condition on the counit.
